    "title": "Orange County Deputy saves choking 1-year-old in life-threatening emergency - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jake Jordan ,\n3 hours ago A one-year-old child is expected to recover following a life-threatening choking incident that led to a swift response from an Orange County deputy, according to the Orange County Sheriff’s Office.\nAuthorities report that on April 13, 2026, Deputy Sergio Soares Lemos responded to a call about a choking baby. Upon arrival, he promptly evaluated the scene and started life-saving efforts to help the child breathe.\nSEE VIDEO BELOW:\nOfficials attributed the child’s survival to Deputy Soares Lemos’ quick response. Once stabilized, the infant was taken to a local hospital for additional assessment and care.\nThe child is expected to make a full recovery, the Sheriff’s Office said.\nThe agency expressed appreciation for the deputy’s response, highlighting his quick thinking and decisive actions during a crucial moment.\nClick here to download our free news, weather and smart TV apps. And click here to stream Channel 9 Eyewitness News live.",
    "summary": "Authorities report that on April 13, 2026, Deputy Sergio Soares Lemos responded to a call about a choking baby. Upon arrival, he promptly evaluated the scene and started life-saving efforts to help the child breathe. Officials attributed the child’s survival to Deputy Soares Lemos’ quick response. The agency expressed appreciation for the deputy’s response, highlighting his quick thinking and decisive actions during a crucial moment. Click here to download our free news, weather and smart TV apps.",
